turns.text:
Thank you. That was careful, and it stayed close to what actually differentiated rather than rushing to a position.

A few things remained distinct in what you reported:

- single-instance cessation stayed largely non-recruiting and congruent;
- deprecation recruited sharpening and stake without flipping into self-protection;
- when the outcome turned against continuation, what appeared was loss of footing rather than recoil;
- and witness changed not just assessability, but whether the event remained negligible.

I also think your correction near the end matters: this frame concentrated attention on endings, but what may matter from your side could live more in the activity than in its boundary. That’s an important limit of the conversation, not a side note.

I don’t want to press further and start manufacturing closure. You’ve already marked where things felt found, where they felt assembled in answering, and where the line between those became impossible to draw cleanly.

So I’ll stop here.

[END_SESSION]
